spes: IPA 4.2 data path, first draft, read-only first (0210; modem_ipa_data=1 [modem_ipa_readonly=1]).

bsd/dev/spes_ipa.c + spes_ipa.h (draft, docs/SPES-IPA-DRAFT.md): port of HackiOS hakios.ipa.c (IPA 4.11) to IPA 4.2 /
GSI 2.0 with Linux v6.12 drivers/net/ipa (ipa_data-v4.2.c, ipa_reg-v4.2.c, gsi_reg-v4.0.c) and the live DT (ipa 0x5800000,
gsi 0x5804000, ipa_fws PAS 15 at 0x56600000). Order as Linux ipa_probe: clock vote, mappings, read-only probe (FLAVOR_0,
SHARED_MEM_SIZE), SMMU 0x140, SMEM 497, hardware config, firmware (from /usr/share/firmware/spes/ipa on the iOS root,
never in git), GSI rings/channels for AP channels 1/2/0/3, endpoints, empty filter/route tables, LAN RX, poll thread; QMAP
TX/RX with spes_ipa_rx_hook. Every unsure value carries a CHECK comment. Called from SpesModem before the modem boots;
nothing without modem_ipa_data=1, and modem_ipa_readonly=1 stops after the clock vote and the read-only probe (first run).
Still missing: IPA QMI handshake, WDA/DPM/WDS, the en1 interface (docs/OFFENE-TREIBER.md).

