+/*
+ * spes (SM6225 "khaje") IPA 4.2 data path between this processor and the modem.
+ * DRAFT - not built, not run. Nothing happens without boot-arg modem_ipa_data=1.
+ *
+ * The IPA ("IP accelerator", hw-ver 0x10 = v4.2 in the live DT) moves IP packets between the modem
+ * and this processor. Its DMA engine, the GSI, has per-execution-environment channels: a channel is a
+ * ring of 16-byte transfer elements (TREs) this processor fills; the GSI writes one 16-byte event per
+ * finished TRE into the channel's event ring. A doorbell register says how far the TRE ring is
+ * filled; the event ring's context register 4 says how far the GSI has written events. No interrupt
+ * is used: a kernel thread polls (as HackiOS hakios.ipa.c does on SM7325).
+ *
+ * AP endpoints/channels for IPA v4.2 (Linux v6.12 drivers/net/ipa/data/ipa_data-v4.2.c):
+ *   command TX  endpoint 6, channel 1  immediate commands to the IPA (tables, header area, zeroing)
+ *   LAN RX      endpoint 8, channel 2  default route and exceptions (looked at, dropped)
+ *   modem TX    endpoint 1, channel 0  IP packets to the modem, behind a 4-byte QMAP header
+ *   modem RX    endpoint 9, channel 3  QMAP-framed packets from the modem, aggregated per buffer
+ * The modem's channels (EE 1: channels 0..3) must be ALLOCATED by this processor on IPA v4.2 (Linux
+ * gsi.c: modem_alloc = version == IPA_VERSION_4_2, GENERIC_CMD ALLOCATE_CHANNEL).
+ *
+ * Init order (Linux ipa_probe(): ipa_config() -> ipa_firmware_load() -> ipa_setup()):
+ *   0  gate, clock vote (RPM SMD "ipa"), register mappings, read-only probe (modem_ipa_readonly=1 stops here)
+ *   1  SMMU identity context for the IPA's AP stream (SID 0x140, live DT ipa_smmu_ap)
+ *   2  SMEM item 497 (0x2000 bytes) for the modem's filter tables (Linux ipa_smem_init())
+ *   3  ipa_config(): hardware config, local-memory canaries, endpoint availability (FLAVOR_0), resource groups
+ *   4  firmware: TrustZone PAS id 15, ipa_fws.mdt/.b00-.b04 into reserved memory 0x56600000 (live DT qcom,ipa_fws)
+ *   5  gsi_setup(): interrupts off, event rings + channels allocated/programmed, modem channels allocated
+ *   6  endpoints programmed, command channel started, ipa_mem_setup(), ipa_table_setup(),
+ *      LAN RX started, default route -> endpoint 8
+ *   7  poll thread; spes_ipa_modem_start() later starts the two modem data channels
+ *
+ * Memory the IPA/GSI reads or writes comes from SpesModem's pool (spes_pool_alloc(): physically
+ * contiguous, below 4 GiB, write-combined = Normal non-cacheable, zeroed), so no cache maintenance is
+ * needed, only barriers before doorbells. The IPA reaches it through an identity SMMU context.
+ * Register addresses: IPA registers at ipa-base + 0x40000 (downstream ipa3 maps ipa-base +
+ * ipa_reg_base_ofst; the ipa_fws ELF has a segment at 0x585e000 inside that window), GSI at gsi-base.
+ *
+ * Every value I am not sure about carries a CHECK comment naming its source.
+ *
+ * Boot-args:  modem_ipa_data=1 (on), modem_ipa_readonly=1 (stop after the read probe),
+ *             modem_ipa_clk=0 (do not vote the IPA clock; assume it is on), modem_ipa_trace=1 (per packet),
+ *             modem_ipa_fw=0 (do not load firmware; only if GSI is already enabled), modem_ipa_mux=N (QMAP mux, 1).
+ */
